        {
          "type": "Health",
          "props": {
            "id": "bulka-health",
            "copy": {
              "health__title": "Health",
              "health__intro": "The streets weren't kind to me.",
              "ui__health_card__prefix": "#"
            },
            "photos": {
              "dog_apartment": {
                "src": "/images/dog_apartment.webp",
                "alt": "At the vet, Lena hugging me",
                "caption": "At the vet. Lena playing emergency"
              },
              "health1": {
                "src": "/images/health1.webp",
                "alt": "My X-ray: spine and bullet next to it",
                "caption": "Belly X-ray. Bullet near the spine — doesn't bother me"
              },
              "health2": {
                "src": "/images/health2.webp",
                "alt": "My X-ray: rear leg",
                "caption": "Leg X-ray. Old injury is visible"
              },
              "cardiology": {
                "src": "/images/cardiology.webp",
                "alt": "Cardiology report from Dr. Filip Božinovski",
                "caption": "Cardiology: dirofilaria immitis Stg II, in treatment"
              }
            },
            "healthItems": [
              {
                "icon": "Crosshair",
                "body": "First, a bad person once shot me with an air pistol. There's a bullet lodged near my spine. It doesn't affect my health and doesn't need to be removed unless it starts to hurt."
              },
              {
                "icon": "Bone",
                "body": "Second, a long time ago I broke my back leg. Nobody treated me, so it healed crookedly, and sometimes after an hour of walking I start to limp. The doctor says it's no big deal, it adds to my charm!"
              },
              {
                "icon": "Worm",
                "body": "Third, I have a heartworm living in my heart. It's at stage two right now — that's the very beginning, the worm is under one centimeter, and my heart is fully clean on ultrasound and ECG (see the report below). Lena has already started driving it out: for the next six months we visit the vet once every two weeks, pay 4000 dinars, and I get an injection plus drops. That's how the worm dies. While I'm in treatment I can't run more than 5 minutes — otherwise I cough."
              },
              {
                "icon": "Ban",
                "body": "Fourth, I can't be spayed until we get rid of the worm. But honestly, I like the ball more than pushy male dogs anyway."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "Conditions",
          "props": {
            "id": "bulka-conditions",
            "copy": {
              "conditions__title": "Conditions",
              "ui__conditions__adoption_title": "Who I go to",
              "conditions__adoption": "Lena says she'll give me to both an apartment and a house, but she won't allow anyone to keep me on a chain.",
              "ui__conditions__support_title": "Support and contact",
              "conditions__communication": "She also says she'd like to stay in touch, or even be friends, with my new people. And she'll take me back if it doesn't click.",
              "conditions__support": "She'll help pay for my treatment and spaying. And on top of that, either she or our friend Ira will take me for boarding whenever you decide to travel. And she can also drive me to the vet in her car, so you don't have to pay for a taxi.",
              "ui__conditions__bonus_title": "Bonus",
              "conditions__perk": "Imagine that, I'm coming as a package deal with two nannies and a personal driver. Not bad for a stray, right?"
            },
            "photos": {
              "ps_family": {
                "src": "/images/photo-set/ps_family.webp",
                "thumbSrc": "/images/photo-set/thumbs/ps_family.webp",
                "alt": "Family photo: Lena, a guy, two cats, and me",
                "caption": "Everyone's holding cats. I lie here and watch the show"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "Questions",
          "props": {
            "id": "bulka-faq",
            "copy": {
              "faq__title": "Stuff people usually ask",
              "faq__subtitle": "Don't see your question? Ping Lena directly — she types faster than I do.",
              "faq__banner_title": "If it doesn't work out, Lena takes me back.",
              "faq__banner_subtitle": "No drama, no conditions, no \"give it another month.\""
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "id": "kids",
                "question": "Are you okay with kids?",
                "answer": "Lena hasn't tested me with kids, I won't lie. But I don't jump, I don't bite, I steer clear of other dogs on the street — the basics are there. Want to play it safe? Come over with the kid, we'll see in person."
              },
              {
                "id": "rental",
                "question": "I'm renting. Can I still adopt you?",
                "answer": "Yes. I'm quiet, I don't wreck things — Lena will vouch for me. If your landlord wants a pet deposit, Lena is happy to talk to them and help explain that I'm not the kind of dog that gets the wallpaper redone."
              },
              {
                "id": "monthly_cost",
                "question": "How much will I spend on you per month?",
                "answer": "Food and a routine vet visit — once we're done with the heartworm. The worm is on Lena's tab, that's not your problem. Money-wise I'm a perfectly average dog — no surprise \"oh and one more illness\" bills."
              },
              {
                "id": "guarantee",
                "question": "What if it doesn't work out?",
                "answer": "Lena takes me back. Free, no drama, no conditions."
              },
              {
                "id": "other_pets",
                "question": "What about other dogs and cats?",
                "answer": "I live with two cats right now and barely notice them: they walk around, I carry on. I don't pick fights with other dogs — if some pushy male comes at me, I just turn away. Not my genre."
              },
              {
                "id": "health",
                "question": "Are you healthy?",
                "answer": "Mostly yes, but there are nuances. The heartworm is being treated, the course is already running. The bullet by my spine just sits there bothering nobody. The crooked leg adds character, doctor's words. Full details are in the Health section — it's all there: the bullet, the leg, the worm."
              },
              {
                "id": "remote",
                "question": "I'm not in Belgrade. Can we do this remotely?",
                "answer": "Depends on how far. Belgrade, Novi Sad and the surrounding area — fine: Lena wants to swing by and visit me sometimes, so she needs to be able to reach me. Rest of the EU — let's hop on a call, we'll figure something out. Another continent, visas, a flight halfway across the planet — straight up: probably not."
              },
              {
                "id": "deadline",
                "question": "When do I need to decide?",
                "answer": "Lena leaves in winter, the exact date is still moving. Nobody's breathing down your neck — but the sooner we figure it out, the calmer it is for everyone, mostly me."
              }
            ]
          }
        },
